<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina's Bansud issues $10 mln short-term debt.</title>
<headline>Argentina's Bansud issues $10 mln short-term debt.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's Banco del Sud SA said Thursday it has issued $10 million in negotiable bonds as part of its $400 million short-term debt program.</p>
<p>Bansud said it issued $10 million in bonds due January 22, 1997, at a price of 97.6787. The bond was totally subscribed by Sud Bank &amp; Trust Company Ltd.</p>
<p>This is the fourth issue under the debt program, putting the total sold at $85 million. Bansud directors approved the debt program on May 29.</p>
<p>-- Axel Bugge, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 3180668</p>
